# Operator-side secrets — generated in CF dashboard, saved on VPS only.
# nginx/certs/ directory is tracked via .gitkeep so the docker-compose
# volume mount has a binding path on a fresh clone.
nginx/certs/origin.pem
nginx/certs/origin.key

# Local scratch — `git diff > diff.txt` for ad-hoc review, never committed.
diff.txt

# Issue #27 — GSD workflow artifacts are local-only.
#
# `.planning/` holds CONTEXT.md / RESEARCH.md / PLAN.md / SUMMARY.md /
# VERIFICATION.md / STATE.md / ROADMAP.md / PROJECT.md / debug sessions /
# todos / discussion logs — historical context for how a phase came
# together. None of it is load-bearing for the running application; the
# squash-merge PR body is the canonical phase record on master (see
# AGENTS.md "Workflow" section).
#
# Old `.planning/` snapshots from previous phases remain in master's
# pre-#27 history; untracking going forward stops new artifacts from
# accumulating in the tree.
#
# Multi-machine sync (laptop + VPS) is out of scope here — the operator
# either copies the directory manually or accepts that planning state
# is single-machine. See AGENTS.md.
.planning/

# Developer-personal dev helpers — each developer ships their own local
# .dev-*.ts/.mjs scripts (e.g. .dev-worker.ts to run the worker handler
# bypassing migrate-at-boot; .dev-oauth-mock.mjs to spin up the OAuth
# mock for interactive sign-in testing; .dev-probe-youtube.ts to drive
# the YouTube adapter directly for diagnostics). These are intentionally
# OUT of source control — they pin a single developer's machine setup
# (admin user_id, API key paths, queue names) and are not portable. The
# canonical scripts (e.g. scripts/dev-mock-oauth.mjs) live under
# scripts/ and ARE committed. Phase 03.0.3 P3 deferred-items.md cites
# .dev-oauth-mock.mjs as an example of why this exclusion matters
# (process.env reads outside config/env.ts are intentional in standalone
# Node scripts; ESLint would otherwise flag every developer's helper).
.dev-*.ts
.dev-*.mjs
